# Every composed layer whose conversion could not be sized is a layer whose own totals cannot be
# differenced. One row: the containment, with the size of each side and whatever falls outside.
#
# Two predicates, one of them inside the other
#   `composition/unsized_conversions.sqlc` keeps the parts whose factor is `absent` or names a
#   derivation. `composition/unsettled.sqlc` keeps those and, in a second arm, the parts whose
#   stated factor has width. So the first is the second with one arm dropped, and its composed
#   layers are inside the second's by construction.
#
# Which is why it is worth a law and not a sentence
#   "By construction" is an argument about two files that nothing reads together, and each states
#   its predicate from scratch without citing the other. Either can grow an arm alone. If the
#   narrow one did, a fusion would have its sum lifted as unsized while the remainder walk still
#   treated its totals as differenceable, and the two suspension grounds would disagree about the
#   same layer with no rule able to see it.
#
# A containment, because equality would fire on a correct filing
#   The second arm is real and populated: a fusion whose factors are all stated but wide is
#   unsettled and has no unsized conversion at all. `every-unsized-conversion/shift-capacity` is
#   the layer on the narrow side; `every-nested-conversion/line-batches`, `line-hours`,
#   `every-unit-cycle/cards` and `merge-holding-composition/compute` are the difference, and they
#   are what an equality here would accuse.
#
# Probe
#   examples/probes runs it as `unsized_conversions_are_unsettled`.
-- composition/unsized_conversions.sqlc projected onto its composed layers, inside composition/unsettled.sqlc.
SELECT a.slug AS law, p.subject, p.holds, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(algebra/roster.sqlc)
) a
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT 'composition/unsized_conversions' AS subject,
           count(*) FILTER (WHERE u.filing IS NULL) = 0 AS holds,
           format('%s composed layer(s) cannot size a conversion, %s cannot be differenced, %s outside%s',
                  count(*), (SELECT count(*) FROM ( :compose(composition/unsettled.sqlc) ) t),
                  count(*) FILTER (WHERE u.filing IS NULL),
                  coalesce(': ' || string_agg(c.composition || '/' || c.composed_layer, ', '
                                              ORDER BY c.composition, c.composed_layer)
                                   FILTER (WHERE u.filing IS NULL), '')) AS detail
    FROM      (
        SELECT DISTINCT composition, composed_layer
        FROM ( :compose(composition/unsized_conversions.sqlc) ) x
    ) c
    LEFT JOIN (
        :compose(composition/unsettled.sqlc)
    ) u ON u.filing = c.composition AND u.layer = c.composed_layer
) p ON true
WHERE a.slug = 'unsized_conversions_are_unsettled'
